            <title xml:id="title_id0b03ce7e" xml:lang="it">VII sonate a cembalo obligato e violino</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_e723baf8">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_id834c0a28">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_idbb642902">
               <p xml:id="idm60">The present collection of seven sonatas for harpsichord and violin appeared the first time in Breitkopf’s catalogue of 1761 and two years later in another catalogue, this time including incipits to the first movements of each sonata. The collection has, however, been lost. It is possible that Breitkopf either acquired the work from the estate of <persName xml:id="idm61" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Carl Gotthelf Gerlach</persName>, cantor at Neukirche in Leipzig, or directly from Scheibe who sent manuscripts of works to Breitkopf – even when he had moved to Denmark (cf. SchW A4:001, A4:Coll.001, A4:Coll.005) – and for which he might have received a fee.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_dbf494b5">
